    "body": "Note that browsers are free to decide how they choose a candidate from `srcset`, and this can differ a bit between browsers. For example, they can have a maximum density so that they [don't load overly large images](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4421), or have some heuristic to decide what to load when the calculated density is in between two candidates, or a \"save data\" user setting is enabled, etc.\r\n\r\nHere's the current logic in chromium: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/parser/html_srcset_parser.cc;l=423",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
